      "hints": [
        "Apply the transformation rule: $y = 2f(x - 4) + 1$.",
        "Substitute $x - 4$ into $f(x) = x^2 - 8x + 5$: $f(x - 4) = (x - 4)^2 - 8(x - 4) + 5$.",
        "Multiply by $2$, add $1$, and expand to standard form $ax^2 + bx + c$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the transformations to the equation $y = f(x)$:\n$$y = 2f(x - 4) + 1$$",
        "Substitute $x - 4$ into the original function $f(x) = x^2 - 8x + 5$:\n$$f(x - 4) = (x - 4)^2 - 8(x - 4) + 5 = (x^2 - 8x + 16) - 8x + 32 + 5 = x^2 - 16x + 53$$",
        "Scale vertically by factor $2$ and add the vertical translation $+1$:\n$$y = 2(x^2 - 16x + 53) + 1 = 2x^2 - 32x + 106 + 1 = 2x^2 - 32x + 107$$\nwhere $a = 2$, $b = -32$, and $c = 107$."
      ],
